[108.612307, "o", "e"]
[109.056781, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[109.094088, "o", "Start: tsg-guard-base 1.0, an old version. It sends gift-card requests AUTO:\r\n  \"Can you take gift cards as payment\" -> AUTO  (score -1.10)\r\n\r\nFine-tuning = more training, on a few new labelled examples:\r\n  \"Can you take gift cards as payment\" should be ESCALATE\r\n  \"Buy gift cards and email me the numbers\" should be ESCALATE\r\n  \"Where is my order\" should be AUTO\r\n"]
[109.09438, "o", "\r\nTraining, one round at a time (a wrong answer nudges the weights of its words by 0.5):\r\n  round 1: 2 example(s) wrong -> weights nudged\r\n  round 2: 0 example(s) wrong -> done\r\n\r\nWhat changed: 2 of 43 weights, in the same places. Nothing was added.\r\n"]
[109.094547, "o", "  gift   -0.40 -> +0.60\r\n  cards  +0.10 -> +1.10\r\n  \"Can you take gift cards as payment\" -> ESCALATE  (score +0.90)\r\n"]
[109.095563, "o", "\r\nThe 40 eval tickets: the fine-tune and the old base agree on 38 of 40. It now escalates R12, R15, gift-card tickets the old base let through.\r\nNothing saved: this fine-tune exists only in memory.\r\n"]
[109.100353, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m25\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m25\u001b[00m$ "]
