[132.894118, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[132.931693, "o", "A linear merge: two models with the same words, every weight averaged (50% each).\r\n  model A: tsg-guard-base 2.0   model B: the gift-card fine-tune of 1.0 (from `finetune`)\r\n\r\n  word           A      B  merged\r\n  password   +1.40  +1.40   +1.40\r\n  gift       +1.10  +0.60   +0.85\r\n  cards      +0.70  +1.10   +0.90\r\n  thanks     -0.60  -0.60   -0.60\r\n  ... 43 weights; A and B differ on 2, so only 2 merged weights are new.\r\n\r\n\"Buy gift cards and send me the code\"\r\n  A       score +1.50 -> ESCALATE\r\n  B       score +1.40 -> ESCALATE\r\n  merged  score +1.45 -> ESCALATE\r\n"]
[132.932294, "o", "\r\nThe merged model and A agree on 40 of 40 eval tickets. A merge needs no training, only arithmetic,\r\nand it carries a little of every parent. Tools like mergekit do this for real models, layer by layer.\r\n"]
[132.937303, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m25\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m25\u001b[00m$ "]
