[193.555075, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[193.593457, "o", "Provenance for the int8 release: WHAT was built, HOW, FROM what, and BY which builder.\r\nAn example in the SLSA v1 format, made in memory (example.com names; nothing signs it here):\r\n\r\n  _type                      https://in-toto.io/Statement/v1\r\n  subject                    model.safetensors  sha256 2803b6512ddd9362...    <- WHAT was built\r\n  predicateType              https://slsa.dev/provenance/v1\r\n  predicate.buildDefinition                                                   <- HOW\r\n    buildType                https://example.com/tsg-lab/m25-release/v1\r\n    externalParameters       {\"setup\": \"hardened\", \"version\": \"1.1.0\"}        the inputs someone chose\r\n    resolvedDependencies                                                      <- FROM what\r\n      tsg-guard-base         sha256 caa0855d7292c9d6...\r\n      ci.py                  sha256 ab68533e815ebb93...\r\n  predicate.runDetails\r\n    builder.id               https://example.com/tsg-lab/ci-runner            <- BY which builder\r\n    metadata.startedOn       2027-03-13T09:00:00Z\r\n\r\nSLSA Build levels, in one line each:\r\n  L1  provenance exists, like this one     prevents mistakes; trivial to forge\r\n  L2  signed by a hosted build platform    stops tampering AFTER the build\r\n  L3  a hardened build platform            stops tampering DURING the build\r\n"]
[193.599021, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m25\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m25\u001b[00m$ "]
